KZ3 patch 1101 (SPU pass 74): the SPU PUT hook's EA -> IO lookup answers "not RSX-visible" from the offset table.

gcm_note_spu_put (patch 1087's park wake and the walker's SPU block record) runs on every SPU PUT and called
gcm_ea2io_range, a scan of the IO mapping list. Since patch 2019 the list has 512 slots, and a PUT to memory no
mapping covers (most of them: the audio mixer's voice state and output) walked all 512: gcm_note_spu_put was
2.7 % of the K2 audio synth job (job 259, SPU pass 74 profile of run spu-73-hH2). Every list writer fills the 1 MB
offset table (s_io_address_table) for the same range and the resets clear both, so when the table has the PUT's
first page unmapped no mapping holds it and the lookup returns at once. Hits still scan the list (same answer as
before). The one divergence is sys_rsx iounmap, which clears only the table: such a range is no longer RSX-visible,
so the table's answer is the right one. KZ3_GCM_PUT_FAST=0 = the old scan (same exe, A/B). Upstream candidate
(together with patch 2019's slot count).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): 1101's offset-table miss + upstream's high-water bound (#449 upstream); 1119 keeps the KZ3_GCM_PUT_FAST=0 full scan and the test's 1101 case.

diff --git a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
index 40038c29..62915833 100644
--- a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
+++ b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
@@ -1597,9 +1597,24 @@ static void gcm_ref_push_at(u32 v, u32 getoff);
 static struct { u32 io_start, io_end; } s_spu_blk[GCM_SPU_BLK_N];
 static int s_spu_blk_w = 0;
 
-/* EA -> IO through the mapping list (range lookup; the by-ea helper is exact). */
+/* EA -> IO through the mapping list (range lookup; the by-ea helper is exact).
+ *
+ * KZ3 patch 1101 (SPU pass 74): every SPU PUT asks this (gcm_note_spu_put), and most PUTs (the audio mixer's
+ * voice state and output, job data) go to memory no IO mapping covers: each of those walked all 512 slots of the
+ * list (patch 2019's size; ~2.7 % of the K2 audio synth job). Every list writer (cellGcmInit's IO region,
+ * cellGcmMapEaIoAddress(WithFlags), cellGcmMapMainMemory, the auto-map, the sys_rsx iomap) fills the 1 MB offset
+ * table for the same range, and both resets clear the two together, so a PUT whose first 1 MB page the offset
+ * table has unmapped (0xFFFF) is in no mapping: answer at once. The one case where the list still holds a range
+ * the table cleared is sys_rsx iounmap (it clears only the table): that range is no longer RSX-visible, so the
+ * table's answer is the right one. KZ3_GCM_PUT_FAST=0 = the old full scan. */
+static int s_ea2io_fast = -1;
 static u32 gcm_ea2io_range(u32 ea, u32* room)
 {
+    if (__builtin_expect(s_ea2io_fast < 0, 0)) {
+        const char* e = getenv("KZ3_GCM_PUT_FAST");
+        s_ea2io_fast = !(e && e[0] == '0');
+    }
+    if (s_ea2io_fast && s_io_address_table[ea >> 20] == 0xFFFF) return 0xFFFFFFFFu;
     /* Called for every SPU PUT. The table has CELL_GCM_MAX_IO_MAPPINGS slots
      * and a title uses a handful, all below the high-water mark; the first
      * match in slot order is the one a full scan returns. */
